WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.002
-Our first guest tonight is

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.502
the United States senator
from Vermont.

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:06.105
Please welcome back to the show
Senator Bernie Sanders.

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.875
How are you, Senator?
-I'm great, Seth. How are you?

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:12.011
-I'm hanging in there.
I want to thank you.

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:14.714
Back in 2020 -- March 2020 --

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.783
our first show
that we did remotely,

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:17.950
you were my first guest then.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.219
You were very dependable
in our time of need.

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:23.088
So I'm mostly just disappointed
we keep having times of need,

00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:25.725
but thank you for continuing
to show up for us.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.359
-My pleasure.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:29.429
-We just went through
a time of the year

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.731
where a lot of people
have vacation,

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.633
took a little time off.

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:37.270
You don't strike me who uses
their down time to relax.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.375
-Well, you know,
in a sense, I don't.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:46.478
You know, these are, Seth,
really tough times

00:00:46.478 --> 00:00:49.815
for our entire country.
You know?

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:53.452
I think maybe the most difficult
times in our lifetimes,

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:55.288
and we got to recognize that.

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.723
And I'm a senator.

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.191
I got work to do,
and I've got to do it.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:01.828
You know, I think
this COVID thing

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.663
is driving everybody crazy.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.265
I know you have to deal with it
yourself

00:01:06.265 --> 00:01:09.469
and were worried about the kids
and worried about isolation

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:13.105
and mental health and stress
and jobs and everything else.

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:17.276
You know, we're fighting now
to preserve American democracy.

00:01:17.276 --> 00:01:20.146
Hopefully, there will be a vote
in the Senate in a week

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:23.182
which will override Republican
efforts to suppress the votes

00:01:23.182 --> 00:01:25.818
and impose
extreme gerrymandering.

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:29.154
And we got to deal
with climate change,

00:01:29.154 --> 00:01:30.723
and we got to deal with
oligarchy

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.491
and income and wealth
inequality.

00:01:32.491 --> 00:01:35.828
So, you know, these are
tough times for the country.

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:39.832
And I think, hopefully,
we're gonna get over this crisis

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:42.268
sooner than later

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:45.505
and move this country in a
direction that it has to go.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:48.974
-One of the toughest things
facing Democrats is

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:50.509
a razor-thin margin.

00:01:50.509 --> 00:01:52.445
Not a lot of wiggle room
within your caucus.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:55.081
Joe Manchin, obviously, has
an outsized influence

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.850
with what is or isn't
going to get passed.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.986
Build Back Better -- Democrats
failed to pass it.

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:03.188
It doesn't seem like Joe Manchin
has a lot of interest

00:02:03.188 --> 00:02:04.790
in working on it anymore.

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.959
Is it now officially dead?

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:09.996
We've heard, a lot of times
over the past year,

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.263
that it was dead.

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:13.666
Is now there any optimism
on your end?

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:16.269
-Well, this is
one of the issues

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:19.439
where we have got to involve
the American people

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:22.207
in doing exactly what they want.

00:02:22.207 --> 00:02:24.744
You know, nobody knows what's
in Build Back Better.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:27.446
You know, they see a big word
out there, a phrase.

00:02:27.446 --> 00:02:30.016
But what it is about is
finally demanding

00:02:30.016 --> 00:02:31.684
that the wealthiest people
in this country

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.119
start paying
their fair share of taxes.

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:35.188
Overwhelming support for that

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:37.757
in the midst of income and
wealth equality.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:40.893
We want to lower the cost
of prescription drugs,

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.795
'cause we pay the highest prices
in the world.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.197
People say, "Do it!"

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:47.033
We want to expand Medicare

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.168
to cover dental, hearing aids,
eyeglasses.

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:50.336
Overwhelming support.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.571
Child care, climate change,

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:54.507
and the need to create
millions of jobs

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:57.075
as we transform
our energy system.

00:02:57.075 --> 00:03:00.546
Affordable housing,
making schools more affordable.

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:03.983
So, all of these issues
are enormously popular,

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.718
and what we have got to do

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:08.054
is create a resonance
with the American people

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:11.991
that demands Joe Manchin
and Kyrsten Sinema

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:15.528
and everybody else,
not to mention Republicans,

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.964
start doing
what the American people want,

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.933
rather than what
wealthy campaign contributors

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:22.701
or the big-money interests
wants.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.338
Seth, one of the things that has
really not been talked about

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:29.074
by the media very much, which
is really quite extraordinary,

00:03:29.074 --> 00:03:31.377
is that
the big-money interests --

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:32.845
and I'm talking about
the drug companies,

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.415
the insurance companies,
the fossil-fuel industry,

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:37.483
and the very wealthy --
are spending

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:41.153
hundreds and hundreds of
millions of dollars right now

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:43.756
to make sure that Congress
does not do

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.725
what the American people
want them to do.

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:48.827
And that talks about
a corrupt political system,

00:03:48.827 --> 00:03:51.797
but it also talks about
the need for the American people

00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:54.300
to stand up and demand
that Congress represent

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.869
their interests
and not just the 1%.

00:03:56.869 --> 00:03:58.337
-I know you've spent
a lot of time

00:03:58.337 --> 00:03:59.906
in a state like West Virginia.

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:02.275
And I think an argument
can be made

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:04.210
that Joe Manchin understands
the voters of that state

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.078
really well,
to be a Democratic senator

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:08.815
in a state that voted so
overwhelmingly for Donald Trump

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:12.352
even though these are things
that would undeniably benefit

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:14.053
the voters of West Virginia.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.588
How do you try to influence
someone

00:04:16.588 --> 00:04:18.625
who turns around and can say,
"Trust me,

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:21.527
I know how this state works
better than the rest of you"?

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:25.098
-Well, I'm sure he does know
his own state very well.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:29.068
In 2016, when
I was running for president,

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:33.506
I think I won
every county in that state.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.641
And you got to,
in West Virginia --

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:37.777
I know that state
a little bit --

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:42.248
and you got a state which is
really struggling economically.

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:44.784
It's an older state.

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:49.689
It's a state where, you know,
you have one economic crisis,

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.224
the opioid crisis,
after another.

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:53.459
So, if you're asking me,
point blank,

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:57.463
do I think that the people
in West Virginia

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.098
want to expand Medicare to cover

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:01.100
dental, eyeglasses,
and hearing aids,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.035
I think they do.

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:06.505
Do they want to make sure

00:05:06.505 --> 00:05:08.841
that the wealthy start paying
their fair share of taxes?

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:12.011
Yeah, I believe they do.
They got childcare crisis.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.513
They got the whole same problems

00:05:14.513 --> 00:05:18.551
that every other state
in this country faces.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:21.487
So why Senator Manchin
holds the views he does,

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:22.989
I'm not quite sure.

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:25.525
But to be honest with you,
I do not think that they reflect

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.894
where the working families
of West Virginia are.

